==English==

===Etymology===
{{unk.}} etymology, 1813.<ref>{{R:Merriam Webster Online}}</ref> Original sense “alcoholic drink”, possibly a variant of {{term|switchel||a drink of molasses and water, often mixed with rum|lang=en}}, attested 1790, itself of uncertain origin.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> Possibly influenced by {{term|fizz|lang=en}}.

In verb sense “to stir”, from {{term|swizzle stick||stick for stirring alcoholic drinks|lang=en}}, itself attested 1859.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪzəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Various kinds of alcoholic drinks.

====Derived terms====
* [[swizzle stick]]

====See also====
* [[cocktail]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb|swizzl|es}}

# To [[stir]] or [[mix]].
#: ''She '''swizzled''' the milk into her coffee.''
# {{context|computing}} To [[permute]] [[bits]].
# {{context|computing|programming|transitive}} To [[convert]] [[portable]] [[symbol]]s or [[position]]s to [[memory]]-dependent [[pointer]]s during [[deserialization]].

